        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Restructure CSS properties which contain contexts]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30613</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30613"/>
        <updated>2026-09-23T17:48:01.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">This is an alternative proposal for <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5349754859" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30437" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30437/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30437">#30437</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Basically, the idea this:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>All values (marked in <code class="notranslate">code</code> in the lists below) are direct sub-features of the CSS property like done everywhere else in the BCD CSS property tree. The support data for these values is whenever the value was first introduced, no matter which context, so their pure first existence.</li>
<li>If consumers want to know when the property and all of their values are usable in a specific context, then they can consult the special context_* behavioral sub-features to get that information</li>
<li>If a value for a given context is not supported at the same time as the context and has existed before for a different context, the value gets also added to the context as a sub-feature. (this is a special case, and you can see it in effect in the second example for <code class="notranslate">stretch</code>).</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This is exercised on two properties: css.properties.align-content and css.properties.align-self.</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto">css.properties.align-content:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>context_block</li>
<li>context_flex</li>
<li>context_grid</li>
<li>context_multicol</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">baseline</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">center</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">end</code> (new from split)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">first baseline</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">flex-end</code> (new)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">flex-start</code> (new)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">last baseline</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">normal</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">safe</code> (new from split)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">space-around</code> (new)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">space-between</code> (new)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">space-evenly</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">start</code> (new from split)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">stretch</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">unsafe</code> (new from split)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto">css.properties.align-self:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>context_flex
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">stretch</code> (different to the original <code class="notranslate">stretch</code> as well as different to context_flex)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>context_grid</li>
<li>context_position_absolute</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">anchor-center</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">auto</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">baseline</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">end</code> (new from split)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">first baseline</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">last baseline</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">normal</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">safe</code> (new from split)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">start</code> (new from split)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">stretch</code> (the original <code class="notranslate">stretch</code> implementation)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">unsafe</code> (new from split)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">I updated the ordering lint to put the contexts at the top, much like we do for workers or for secure_context_required.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto"><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5349754859" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30437" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30437/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30437">#30437</a></p>]]></content>
