        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 150 adds support for the <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-page-3/#page-margin-safety" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">page-margin-safety</code></a> descriptor of the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@page" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">@page</code></a> at-rule. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5515971464527872" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5515971464527872</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a data point for the new descriptor, but I've also taken this opportunity to rearrange the existing data points to make the descriptors and sub-at-rules all sit together by adding some prefixes to the keys.</p>

